= Python =

== Scope ==
This category covers the Python programming language as a language, runtime, implementation ecosystem, and software-development environment.

== Includes ==
Python syntax and semantics, its data model, standard-language concepts, interpreters such as CPython, typing, packaging and environments, testing, concurrency/async behavior, performance and memory behavior, tooling, and Python-specific ecosystem practices when they help explain how the language is used or implemented.

== Excludes / boundary ==
General programming, algorithm, software-engineering, data-science, or scientific concepts should not be placed here merely because Python can be used to implement them. A third-party package belongs here when the Python ecosystem/runtime relationship is materially relevant, not simply because the package happens to be written in Python.

== Category role ==
'''Technical topic navigation category.''' Python is not a top-level Domain. It is a focused knowledge surface within Computer science and may connect to many applied fields.

